; FILED: set! of a function PARAMETER from a `do` body — NATIVE is the wrong
; side here. R7RS: the three writes mutate the binding, so n ends at 13.
; native -r : 10   (wrong — the do body's writes do not reach the parameter)
; vm        : 13   (correct — `do` compiles inline, so set! is a direct store)
; Native's named-let form of the same program IS correct (13), so this is
; specific to native's `do` lowering. Native codegen is not VM-owned.
(define (f n) (do ((i 0 (+ i 1))) ((= i 3)) (set! n (+ n 1))) n)
(display (f 10))
(newline)
